WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.652
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:09.501
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:14.543
Unit three: Articles (a/an/the). Today you will choose between a, an and the.

4
00:00:14.843 --> 00:00:17.426
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:21.425
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:22.971
A.

7
00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:27.457
A means the word we use before a singular consonant sound.

8
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.272
I have a pen.

9
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:31.897
Your turn. Say: A.

10
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:35.444
A.

11
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:36.848
An.

12
00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.651
An means the word we use before a vowel sound.

13
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.448
She eats an orange.

14
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.971
Your turn. Say: An.

15
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:48.614
An.

16
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:49.980
The.

17
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.970
The means the word for a specific thing that we both know.

18
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:56.130
The book is on the table.

19
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:59.067
Your turn. Say: The.

20
00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:02.714
The.

21
00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.370
Apple.

22
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:08.138
Apple means a round fruit that grows on trees.

23
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.657
I eat an apple every day.

24
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.531
Your turn. Say: Apple.

25
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:17.228
Apple.

26
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:18.950
Umbrella.

27
00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.111
Umbrella means something you hold above your head when it rains.

28
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.205
Take an umbrella today.

29
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:28.063
Your turn. Say: Umbrella.

30
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:31.959
Umbrella.

31
00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:33.358
Book.

32
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.733
Book means pages with words that you read.

33
00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:38.527
This is a good book.

34
00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:41.351
Your turn. Say: Book.

35
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.073
Book.

36
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:46.899
Specific.

37
00:01:47.883 --> 00:01:51.566
Specific means one particular thing, not just any thing.

38
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.894
The red pen is specific.

39
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:57.043
Your turn. Say: Specific.

40
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.157
Specific.

41
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:02.720
General.

42
00:02:03.717 --> 00:02:06.761
General means not one particular thing, but any thing.

43
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.955
A pen is a general word.

44
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.959
Your turn. Say: General.

45
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:15.755
General.

46
00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:20.392
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.306
Visal, do we say 'a apple' or 'an apple'?

48
00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:37.685
We say 'an apple'. We use an before a vowel sound: an apple, an umbrella. We use a before a consonant sound: a book, a pen.

49
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:40.191
And when do we use 'the'?

50
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:50.867
We use the for something specific that both people know. Compare: I have a book, then Please open the book on the table.

51
00:02:51.983 --> 00:02:54.679
Is the first sound or the first letter important?

52
00:02:55.783 --> 00:03:05.471
The sound is important. We say 'an hour' because hour starts with a vowel sound, and 'a university' because it starts with a y sound.

53
00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:08.389
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.119
Grammar focus: Articles: a and an and the.

55
00:03:13.419 --> 00:03:14.757
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.823
a book (any book)

57
00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:19.298
an apple (vowel sound)

58
00:03:20.183 --> 00:03:21.986
the book (a specific book)

59
00:03:22.933 --> 00:03:30.415
Use a before a consonant sound, an before a vowel sound, and the for a specific thing. The sound matters, not only the letter.

60
00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.371
Be careful! Don't say: She eats a apple.

61
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.147
Say: She eats an apple.

62
00:03:38.447 --> 00:03:40.481
Use an before a vowel sound.

63
00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.919
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:46.071
A Day at School.

65
00:03:46.371 --> 00:03:48.800
I have a book and an umbrella in my bag.

66
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.287
Today, an old teacher gave us a test.

67
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.147
The test was easy, and the students were happy.

68
00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:58.750
I ate an apple at lunch.

69
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:01.849
Then I read the book that my friend gave me.

70
00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:07.040
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:07.883 --> 00:04:09.360
She has blank umbrella.

72
00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.176
A, a. B, an. C, the.

73
00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:17.060
The answer is B: an.

74
00:04:18.217 --> 00:04:19.543
I need blank pen.

75
00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:22.614
A, an. B, a. C, two.

76
00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.783
The answer is B: a.

77
00:04:28.917 --> 00:04:31.894
Please close blank door. (a specific door)

78
00:04:32.194 --> 00:04:35.070
A, a. B, an. C, the.

79
00:04:38.633 --> 00:04:40.180
The answer is C: the.

80
00:04:41.317 --> 00:04:42.863
Which phrase is correct?

81
00:04:43.163 --> 00:04:47.188
A, an hour. B, a hour. C, an university.

82
00:04:50.733 --> 00:04:52.803
The answer is A: an hour.

83
00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:56.844
According to the reading, what did the writer eat at lunch?

84
00:04:57.144 --> 00:05:00.449
A, an apple. B, a book. C, an umbrella.

85
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.116
The answer is A: an apple.

86
00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.347
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:11.183 --> 00:05:13.125
When do we use 'an' instead of 'a'?

88
00:05:21.917 --> 00:05:23.359
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:23.659 --> 00:05:38.980
We use an instead of a when the next word starts with a vowel sound. For example, we say an apple, an umbrella and an hour. We use a when the next word starts with a consonant sound, such as a book or a pen.

90
00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.874
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:41.783 --> 00:05:46.154
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and articles: a and an and the.

92
00:05:46.454 --> 00:05:50.546
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:05:50.846 --> 00:05:53.371
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

94
00:05:53.671 --> 00:05:56.613
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

